Today is Friday and I am working in the office.
Vikram comes to my desk.
He is a software tester and he has tested my code.
Vikram says, "Maya, I have checked your first code."
I ask, "Is there any problem, Vikram?"
He replies, "I have seen some small mistakes in it."
"But do not worry, you have done very good work."
He shows me my mistakes on my computer.
I listen to him carefully.
His eye is very sharp and he is a good tester.
I say, "Thank you Vikram, you have caught this very quickly."
I immediately change my code.
I write a few lines again.
Then I say to Vikram, "I have fixed the code now."
Vikram runs the code again.
He smiles and says, "Now this is absolutely correct."
I am very happy that I have completed my first task.
